# Book a demo — copy to .env for local development, and add the same values in
# Vercel → Project Settings → Environment Variables.

# Where bookings go: the "Catch Hook" URL from the trigger of the "Creative Seat
# Book Demo Form" Zap (Webhooks by Zapier). The Zap adds the visitor to HubSpot
# and puts the demo in the calendar with them invited. Without it, production
# refuses bookings rather than lose them (and offers the studio's email), and
# `npm run dev` answers with sample bookings that go nowhere.
ZAPIER_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Where availability comes from: the mia calendar API
# (github.com/ElevenAndOne/mia-calendar-api), the same one miacreate.ai uses.
# It reads the demo calendar's free/busy from Google, so this site holds no
# Google credentials. Point it at another deployment to use another calendar.
# CALENDAR_API_URL=https://mia-calendar-api.vercel.app

# When demos can happen, in the studio's time zone — keep it in step with the
# calendar API's working hours. Visitors see the slots in their own time zone.
# Weekends are always closed; to close a weekday (a public holiday), add an
# all-day event marked Busy to the demo calendar.
BOOKING_TIME_ZONE=Africa/Johannesburg
BOOKING_HOURS=09:00-17:00
# Breathing room kept clear either side of existing meetings.
BOOKING_BUFFER_MINUTES=0
